 ## Background
-Bonxai was introduced as a replacement for the `VoxelHashMap` in the KISS-ICP project by the PRBonn group [S1, unofficial]. The motivation was to move away from simple hash tables to a more appropriate and flexible data structure for representing 3D space, enabling future extensions like TSDF registration [S1, unofficial]. The library was chosen for being well-maintained, header-only, and integrated with the ROS ecosystem [S1, unofficial]. Benchmarks were conducted using `heaptrack` for memory analysis and comparing against `VoxelHashMap` [S1, unofficial].
+Bonxai was introduced as a replacement for the `VoxelHashMap` in the KISS-ICP project by the PRBonn group [S1, unofficial]. The motivation was to move away from simple hash tables to a more appropriate and flexible data structure for representing 3D space, enabling future extensions like TSDF registration [S1, unofficial]. The library was chosen for being well-maintained, header-only, and having no additional dependencies [S1, unofficial]. Benchmarks were conducted using `heaptrack` for memory analysis and comparing against `VoxelHashMap` [S1, unofficial].
 
